"Document: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-liammagnier-Developer-project-juno/bfdee244-0283-4629-a3f4-3c603fc89908/scratchpad/audit/02-AUDIT-MAC.md (about 12.7k words, main @ d0997af2). Key conclusions:\n\n1. The Mac has three artifact surfaces that don't know about each other: a chat dock built only from the message's tag text, an Artifacts library built from synced rows, and a Design screen. All three use one `DesktopDesignSurface`, which runs the bundled web editor in a WKWebView. The editor, the bridge between it and the app, and the preview sandbox are sound and a good base for a merge.\n2. The main problem is silent data loss:\n   - Saves take the base version from whatever sync last delivered, so a save can overwrite newer changes (H5).\n   - Unsaved design and library drafts are dropped without a prompt (H6, M1).\n   - The Swift design model has no `cornerSmoothing` field, so every Mac or iPhone save removes it (H4).\n   - On the server, editing an earlier message, regenerating, or deleting a conversation hard-deletes artifacts (X1, X3, X4).\n3. The chat dock can't open designs made in chat (H1). It never picks up a revision that reuses the same identifier (H2). HTML that loads CDN scripts, fonts or images renders broken on the Mac and iPhone (H9).\n4. The editor that shipped in Mac 1.6.0 is 11 commits stale, and only the iOS release checks the bundle (M5). Its stylesheet lacks the shared UI classes (H7) and its palette is wrong (M6). Its layout hides the inspector at the default window size (H8). Export and image insertion don't work (M7, M8).\n5. One unknown-type or oversized record empties the whole native library, and the Design screen then falsely says \"No designs yet\" (H3). This can happen today, because chat designs are size-checked before a 5\u20136.5\u00d7 expansion. It will hit every installed build as soon as a Doc or Slides type ships.\n6. Work deliverables barely show up natively. The live list drops every cloud-run file (H10) and the stored list is read only once per task (H11). The iPhone shows nothing. Tasks started on the Mac can't be reached on the web (H12). The web chat has also lost its Office/PDF downloads (X9).\n7. Motion tokens are excellent, but the Mac surfaces are nearly static. The dock still slides with Reduce Motion on, and enters on the ease-out-expo curve the web dropped.\n8. The Liquid Glass branch fixes none of these defects. It promotes Design to a sidebar row next to Artifacts. It also routes native regenerate into the server's artifact-deleting path.\n9. Scorecard: capability 4, UX 3, visual design 4, motion 4, reliability 3, code health 5.\n10. Merge order:\n    - Server: separate artifact lifetime from messages and keep one id per artifact.\n    - Ship native decoding that tolerates unknown types before any new type exists.\n    - Generate the Swift schema, CSS and bundle, gated by CI.\n    - Move native saves to the per-edit transactions route and have the editor pick up newer versions.\n    - Back the chat dock with the stored row.\n    - Fold the Design screen into Artifacts.\n    - Then share links, comments and runtime parity.\n\nI read the code to settle three points where the reports disagreed. The dock slides under Reduce Motion (`DesktopArtifactCanvas.swift:433-439`). The iPhone library can edit designs (`JunoMobileWorkspaceViews.swift:2062-2067`). The native decoder rejects the compact design form chat produces (`DesignDocumentCodec.swift:44-50`)."